Fix a real upstream build bug (not an AXOS feature): release/src/router/Makefile's
`rc:` and `bwdpi_source:` prerequisite lists only build the `sys_util` and
`gen_util` static libraries when BOTH the chip family (RTCONFIG_HND_ROUTER_AX_675X /
_6756 / _6710 / RTCONFIG_BCM_502L07P2) AND RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD are "y" —
`$(if $(and $(RTCONFIG_HND_ROUTER_AX_6756),$(RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD)),sys_util
gen_util)`. But release/src/router/rc/Makefile's own LDFLAGS
(`ifeq ($(or $(HND_ROUTER_AX_675X),$(HND_ROUTER_AX_6756),$(HND_ROUTER_AX_6710),
$(BCM_502L07P2)),y) ... -lgen_util ... -lsys_util`) link against both
libraries whenever the chip family matches, with no RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD
check at all. For GT-AX6000 (chip 4912, RTCONFIG_HND_ROUTER_AX_6756=y) this
mismatch only surfaces once RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD is actually off (see
build.sh and 0a1cab5/3897483): the linker looks for -lsys_util/-lgen_util
because the chip family requires them, but the libraries themselves were
never built because their prerequisite additionally required hostapd.

Confirmed via a real build attempt: `make gt-ax6000` (with
RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD genuinely off — see the firmware/build.sh command-line
overrides, which pass each flag as truly empty, not "n", so this generated
.config actually reflects them as off) fails linking `rc` with "cannot find
-lgen_util" / "cannot find -lsys_util".

Fix: drop the RTCONFIG_BRCM_HOSTAPD requirement from these four prerequisite
clauses (both in the `rc:` and `bwdpi_source:` targets), so sys_util/gen_util
build whenever the chip family alone calls for them — matching what
rc/Makefile's LDFLAGS already assume. This is a general Makefile
inconsistency (the two lists were never meant to disagree), not something
specific to disabling hostapd for this model.

`git apply --check`-verified against the pinned tag (3004.388.9). Not yet
verified past that point in a completed build — see docs/build-environment.md
and docs/ROADMAP.md.

